                <pb facs="0233" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg177"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Joint resolution for the relief of Edward O’M.
                        Condon</hi>.</head>
                <p>Whereas Edward O’M. Condon, a citizen of the United States, is now, and has been
                    for some time closely confined in prison under the sentence of a British court;
                    and whereas an earnest and profound desire, evidenced by resolutions of State
                    legislatures, and petitions numerously signed and addressed to Congress, is
                    entertained by a large and respectable portion of the people of the United
                    States that he should be speedily released: Therefore,</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved by the Senate and House of Representatives of
                        the United States of America in Congress assembled</hi>, That the President
                    of the United States be, and he is hereby, requested to take such steps as in
                    his judgment may tend to obtain the pardon or release of the said Edward O’M.
                    Condon from imprisonment.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Approved <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-07-07">July 7, 1876</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
